# Page objects

- Own semantic locators and user operations; specs own steps and assertions.
- Accept typed inputs from `src/data/`; keep routes named and configuration in `src/config/`.
- Never import `expect`, fixtures, `test.step`, or `test.info`.
- Return `Locator`, not booleans, so specs can use auto-retrying assertions.

```typescript
// ❌ CSS locator and assertion hidden in the page object
async verifySubmitted(): Promise<void> {
  await expect(this.page.locator('#success')).toHaveText('Thanks!')
}

// ✅ Verified semantic locator exposed to the spec
getSendButton(): Locator {
  return this.page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Send' })
}

getAlert(text: string): Locator {
  return this.page.getByRole('alert').filter({ hasText: text })
}

async fillForm(input: ContactFormInput): Promise<void> {
  await this.getFirstNameInput().fill(input.firstName)
  await this.getEmailInput().fill(input.email)
}

// ✅ Spec owns the assertion
await expect(contactPage.getAlert(ContactCopy.confirmation), 'Confirmation should appear').toHaveText(
  ContactCopy.confirmation,
)
```
